# Build and test (iOS)

**Canonical procedure:** `AGENTS.md > Build and test`. That section is the single source of truth for all agent tools. Follow it exactly; do not duplicate it here.

## Quick reference — four steps in order

After any substantive Swift, SwiftUI, or Xcode change, run from the repo root:

1. `make format` — auto-fix formatting
2. `make lint-fix` — auto-fix correctable lint, then strict gate
3. `make build` — bare compile (no test runner); catches errors fast
4. `make test` — full suite on one iPhone simulator (only after 1–3 pass)

**One command for all four:** `make gate` (alias `bash scripts/gate.sh`) runs the four steps in order, logs to `tmp/gate.log`, and stops at the first failure. To wait on a CI run, use `bash scripts/wait_ci.sh <run-id> [pr#]` — never a hand-written `until … sleep … done` loop.

See `AGENTS.md > Build and test` for simulator pinning (`SIMULATOR_UDID`, `SIMULATOR_NAME`), deployment-target rules, scheme name, and rationale.
